{
  "info": {
    "_postman_id": "voltaras-meter-reading-2026-0001",
    "name": "VOLTARAS - Meter Reading Service",
    "description": "API tests for the VOLTARAS Meter Reading Service.\n\nSETUP\n1. Start Eureka, Auth, User, Meter Reading, and the API Gateway (http://localhost:8080).\n2. Register a CONSUMER and an ADMIN user via POST /api/auth/register (public route) — the auth service only seeds roles, not users.\n3. Open the Authentication folder and replace the placeholder email/password in both login requests with your registered accounts.\n4. Run 'Login (Consumer)' and 'Login (Admin)' first — the JWT is stored automatically in the collection variables accessToken / adminAccessToken.\n\nDo NOT add X-User-Id / X-User-Email / X-User-Role headers manually — the API Gateway validates the JWT and injects them automatically.\n\nFolders: Authentication · Consumer Meter Readings · Admin Meter Readings · Negative Tests\n\nEvery folder is self-contained and can be run independently (after Authentication): the Admin folder starts with a setup request that creates a fresh reading, and the negative tests create and verify their own readings via chained requests, so no cross-request ordering is required. Meter numbers use Postman dynamic variables ({{$guid}} / Date.now()) so the collection can be re-run without duplicate-reading conflicts.",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
  "variable": [
    { "key": "baseUrl", "value": "http://localhost:8080" },
    { "key": "accessToken", "value": "" },
    { "key": "adminAccessToken", "value": "" },
    { "key": "readingId", "value": "" }
  ],
  "item": [
    {
      "name": "Authentication",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Login (Consumer)",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('Status 200 OK', function () { pm.response.to.have.status(200); });",
                  "pm.test('Response is JSON', function () { pm.response.to.be.json; });",
                  "",
                  "const jsonData = pm.response.json();",
                  "",
                  "pm.test('JWT token is present', function () {",
                  "    pm.expect(jsonData.token).to.not.be.undefined;",
                  "    pm.expect(jsonData.role).to.eql('CONSUMER');",
                  "});",
                  "",
                  "pm.collectionVariables.set('accessToken', jsonData.token);"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              { "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }
            ],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"email\": \"consumer@voltaras.com\",\n  \"password\": \"ReplaceWithYourPassword\"\n}"
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/auth/login"
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "Login (Admin)",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('Status 200 OK', function () { pm.response.to.have.status(200); });",
                  "pm.test('Response is JSON', function () { pm.response.to.be.json; });",
                  "",
                  "const jsonData = pm.response.json();",
                  "",
                  "pm.test('JWT token with ADMIN role is present', function () {",
                  "    pm.expect(jsonData.token).to.not.be.undefined;",
                  "    pm.expect(jsonData.role).to.eql('ADMIN');",
                  "});",
                  "",
                  "pm.collectionVariables.set('adminAccessToken', jsonData.token);"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              { "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }
            ],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"email\": \"admin@voltaras.com\",\n  \"password\": \"ReplaceWithYourPassword\"\n}"
